Three boundaries run through this, and they matter more than the licenses do.

The decoded card data is the awkward one. The instruction bands in
09_programs/ and the hole patterns in 10_emulator/web/decks.js are my reading
of Radon's scans, and the reading is my work: the grid fitting, the polarity
argument, the deck order and its cross-checks. What sits underneath is his.
He scanned 222 metal cards and put them up in the thread named in the README,
under no license at all. So I place my transcription and analysis under CC BY
4.0, and I do not claim, and cannot grant, anything about the scans
themselves. If you build on this, credit him as well as me.

08_tangible_media/ is not mine at all. The photograph of the unpunched card
and the two archived HTML pages are John Wallace's, Creative Commons
BY-NC 4.0, and his notice sits next to them in 08_tangible_media/LICENSE. Note
the NC: that folder cannot be used commercially, whatever the MIT License in
LICENSE says about the rest.

